{
  "an7.58:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 7.58 ",
  "an7.58:0.2": "6. The Undeclared Points ",
  "an7.58:0.3": "Nothing to Hide ",
  "an7.58:1.1": "“Mendicants, there are four areas where the Realized One has nothing to hide, and three ways he is irreproachable. ",
  "an7.58:1.2": "What are the four areas where the Realized One has nothing to hide? ",
  "an7.58:1.3": "His bodily behavior is pure. ",
  "an7.58:1.4": "So the Realized One has no bodily misconduct to hide, thinking: ",
  "an7.58:1.5": "‘Don’t let others find this out about me!’ ",
  "an7.58:2.1": "His verbal behavior is pure. ",
  "an7.58:2.2": "So the Realized One has no verbal misconduct to hide, thinking: ",
  "an7.58:2.3": "‘Don’t let others find this out about me!’ ",
  "an7.58:3.1": "His mental behavior is pure. ",
  "an7.58:3.2": "So the Realized One has no mental misconduct to hide, thinking: ",
  "an7.58:3.3": "‘Don’t let others find this out about me!’ ",
  "an7.58:4.1": "His livelihood is pure. ",
  "an7.58:4.2": "So the Realized One has no wrong livelihood to hide, thinking: ",
  "an7.58:4.3": "‘Don’t let others find this out about me!’ ",
  "an7.58:5.1": "These are the four areas where the Realized One has nothing to hide. ",
  "an7.58:6.1": "What are the three ways the Realized One is irreproachable? ",
  "an7.58:6.2": "The Realized One has explained the teaching well. ",
  "an7.58:6.3": "I see no reason for anyone—whether ascetic, brahmin, god, Māra, or the Divinity, or anyone else in the world—to legitima